WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.322 --> 00:00:12.394
In this lesson, you will learn to run your working day from the My Day screen: finishing tasks, changing their status, and adding your own tasks in about ten seconds.

2
00:00:13.257 --> 00:00:26.481
Open My Day first thing every morning. The banner shows your streak, your points this week, and your level. The ring shows how many tasks you have finished today.

3
00:00:27.389 --> 00:00:39.365
Here, your week in numbers shows last week's points, tasks done, on-time percentage and stand-ups. It also shows your rank among your colleagues.

4
00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:50.690
Scroll down. Focus now shows the one task to do next. Overdue tasks appear in red, and they come first.

5
00:00:51.552 --> 00:01:07.128
To change a task's status without opening it, use the drop-down on the right. The choices are To Do, In Progress, Blocked, In Review and Done. Let us set this task to In Progress.

6
00:01:07.988 --> 00:01:19.940
If you are waiting for someone else, choose Blocked, and write the reason. The person who assigned the task is told straight away, and you avoid a late penalty.

7
00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:28.733
When a task is finished, click Mark done. You earn points straight away, and the ring fills up.

8
00:01:29.595 --> 00:01:39.219
Now let us add a task of your own. Click New task at the top right. Or press N on your keyboard.

9
00:01:40.084 --> 00:01:53.356
Type the task in plain words. KalamDesk understands at-name for who, P one to P four for priority, and words like today, tomorrow or five p m for the deadline.

10
00:01:54.221 --> 00:02:07.469
See the small chips underneath? They show what KalamDesk understood: the task, who it is for, the priority and the deadline. Click Add task to save it.

11
00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:14.978
Your new task is now in your list. Click its title to open the task.

12
00:02:15.834 --> 00:02:23.994
Here, you can break the work into steps. Type a step in the checklist box, and click Add.

13
00:02:24.855 --> 00:02:37.719
Tick a step off when it is done. Use the comment box to ask a question, or give an update. Type at-name to mention a colleague, and they will be notified.

14
00:02:38.584 --> 00:02:49.240
You can also attach photos and documents, up to ten megabytes each, and the activity list at the bottom records every change automatically.

15
00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:59.892
That is My Day. Next, you will learn the daily stand-up, and how to see your work on the board, the list and the calendar.
